:[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nI'm new to Godot and have only ever used: `Godot v 4.3.stable.ofiicial`\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.26100 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - AMD Ryzen 7 9800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing GDScript:\nCreating a `tween` and then calling `.tween_property(,)` with a comma `(,)` as the only parameter instantly crashes Godot. \nThis happens in the editor as I'm writing the code i.e. not at runtime.\nHappens consistently across projects and scripts.\n\n**Code sample:**\n```gdscript\nvar tween = get_tree().create_tween()\ntween.tween_property(,)\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a GDScript on e.g. a Node2D\n2. Write this code inside a function (or anywhere actually): \n```gdscript\nvar tween = get_tree().create_tween()\ntween.tween_property()\n```\n3. Add a comma in the `tween_property()` call like so: `tween_property(,)`\n4. Observe the crash :-/\n\nHere's a short recording of the bug where you can see the editor crashing to desktop at the end:\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/650f35a1-fbc4-422b-af5b-b6c63f12f056\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A - the issue is reproducible in a brand new project","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/